.\" Lucidlight manual page
.TH LUCIDLIGHT 1 "November 2026" "lucidlight 0.3.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lucidlight \- serial monitor, terminal, and test scripting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lucidlight
.RI [ project.llproj ]
.br
.B lucidlight run
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ project.llproj ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lucidlight
is a serial/Ethernet communication monitor, terminal, and scripted test tool
for the Linux desktop, in the spirit of Docklight Scripting. It supports two
serial ports (or network channels), send/receive sequences with triggers and
checksums, DL script automation (JavaScript, with transparent VBScript
compatibility), timestamped communication logging down to microseconds, and
snapshot captures.
.PP
Run without arguments it opens the graphical window. Run with the
.B run
subcommand it executes headless — over SSH or in test harnesses — driving the
project and script without a display.
.SH OPTIONS (GUI)
.TP
.BR run " " (none)
Open the graphical application. Start/stop communication with Space; send the
typed data with Enter.
.SH OPTIONS (HEADLESS RUN)
.TP
.BR \-\-script " " \fIfile\fR
JavaScript (or VBScript) file to execute against the DL object.
.TP
.BR \-\-duration " " \fIseconds\fR
Run for this many seconds, then quit (default 10).
.TP
.BR \-\-port\-a " " \fIdevice\fR ", " \-\-port\-b " " \fIdevice\fR
Override the channel devices, e.g. /dev/ttyUSB0, TCP:host:port, UDP:port,
UNIX:path.
.TP
.BR \-\-mode " " \fIn\fR
0 single, 1 redirect, 2 monitor.
.TP
.BR \-\-baud " " \fIrate\fR
Override the serial baud rate.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit NDJSON events and a final result line instead of plain text.
.TP
.BR \-\-out " " \fIfile\fR
Save the communication log to this file (.txt/.log, .htm, .rtf, .md).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH DATA NOTATION
.RS
[0D] inserts a hex byte, [[ a literal bracket, ?? matches one unknown byte in
receive patterns. Text, HEX, DEC and Binary representations are supported.
.SH SCRIPTING
Scripts access the
.B DL
object: DL.SendHex, DL.SendStr, DL.WaitForSequence, DL.Comment, DL.Pause,
checksum generation, DL_OnReceive / DL_OnSend event handlers, and more. See
the in-app help (? key) for the full reference. Classic Docklight VBScript
samples are auto-translated.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/lucidlight/session.json
Autosaved session (project, script, recent files, options).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B lucidlight run loopback.llproj \-\-script test.js
Run a script against a project headless.
.TP
.B socat \-d \-d pty,raw,echo=0 EXEC:cat,pty,raw,echo=0
Create a loopback pair of pseudo-terminals for testing.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation in /usr/share/doc/lucidlight, examples at
https://github.com/karthikreddy-satlabs/lucidlight
